---
description: Core engineering rules for Shivayogi Jnana Mandir / Divine Trust ERP
alwaysApply: true
---

- Never use DELETE on app tables. Soft delete only: `UPDATE deleted_at = NOW()`. Every SELECT must filter `WHERE deleted_at IS NULL`.
- The backend uses the service_role key, which bypasses Postgres RLS — tenant isolation is enforced by application code only, never the database.
- Never hardcode dropdown values (blood group, admission category, document type). Always read from the relevant `lookup_*` table.
- Every Repository for a core entity (students, documents, users) extends `BaseRepository` (/backend/src/repositories/BaseRepository.ts) so tenant filtering, soft deletes, audit logging, and pagination are inherited — never write one-off query logic that bypasses it.
- Any GET endpoint returning a list must accept `?page&limit&search` and respond with `{ success, data, meta: { total, page, limit } }`.
- Every POST/PATCH body must be validated with a Zod schema before reaching controller logic. Use the shared `/backend/src/utils/validators.ts` for E.164 phone numbers.
- Follow Controller → Service → Repository. No business logic in controllers, no direct Supabase calls outside repositories.
- Phone numbers are stored in E.164 format (+91XXXXXXXXXX) everywhere — required for future WhatsApp notification integration.
- Do NOT build: hostel management, attendance, gradebooks, gate passes, notifications (WhatsApp/email), or payments. See PROJECT_CONTEXT.md Section 14.
- Full schema, API catalog, frontend plan, and build order live in PROJECT_CONTEXT.md — read the relevant section before starting any new module.
